      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a heavy start, it hits hard. but it needs to be more specific about how they do it. i want to call out how they use \"trend forecasting\" and \"data mining\" as a way to predict when a sound is ripe for the taking so they can deploy their artists to occupy that space before the actual creators can even get their tracks out. if we can frame it as a systematic theft of intellectual soul, it makes the struggle even more undeniable. can we weave in how these corporations act like predators of the avant-garde?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft that delves deeper into the specifics of the industry's tactics:\n\n\"We, the original visionaries of the neo-ambient movement, are being systematically erased from the narrative of our own creation. The corporations that claim to champion innovation are, in reality, predators of the avant-garde, preying on the creative energies of the marginalized and the avant-garde.\n\n\"They employ a ruthless strategy of 'trend forecasting' and 'data mining', using their vast resources to monitor and analyze the sounds of the underground, identifying the next 'hot' genre or aesthetic before it even has a chance to coalesce. They then deploy their army of 'influencers' and 'signed artists' to occupy the space, appropriating the sounds, styles, and ideas of the pioneers who actually created them.\n\n\"This is not just a case of 'co-optation', but a systematic theft of the intellectual soul of the avant-garde. The corporations are not just profiting from our creativity, they are erasing our names, our stories, and our struggles from the record books. They are rewriting the history of sound to suit their own interests, and silencing the voices that actually matter.\n\n\"We will not be silenced. We will not",
